# REQ-012: Filing

**Priority:** Must Have
**Effort:** Low (manual filing — pre-built ✅)
**Risk:** High (mandatory fields enforce data quality; incorrect metadata could misattribute documents in patient record)
**Depends On:** REQ-011 (Patient Matching), REQ-001 (Unified Inbound Document Inbox), REQ-009 (Audit Trail)

> ⚠️ **Implementation note:**
> - **Manual metadata capture** (including mandatory field enforcement for patient match, document type, date of care, date received, and document title) is already implemented as a reusable component. **Do not re-implement.** Integrate the existing component.

---

## User Story

As a practice administrator,
I need to file inbound documents against a patient record with complete, accurate metadata,
So that documents are correctly attributed, findable, and clinically safe to act upon.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Where metadata is fully embedded in the inbound document (e.g. from MESH, Docman Connect, structured source) and the patient is auto-matched, the document is automatically routed to the tasking queue following the practice's routing rules — no manual filing action required. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Documents auto-routed to tasking are immediately visible on the patient record with a **Provisional** status, indicating they are awaiting processing through the tasking mechanism. Provisional status is cleared when the document has been actioned through tasking. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Where the patient match was not automatically confirmed (low-confidence path — see REQ-011), the user must complete the patient match before the document is routed to tasking. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The user can review and amend any auto-populated metadata field before filing. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The patient details area in filing includes Date of Birth (DOB). *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Filing metadata includes both **Date of care** and **Date received** fields. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The following fields are mandatory and must be completed before a document can be filed: patient match, document type, date of care, date received, document title. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] A document cannot be filed if any mandatory field is missing — the system must block submission and indicate which fields are incomplete. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] All filed documents are assigned a unique document ERN on filing. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Filing action is audited. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Completing filing updates the corresponding EMIS Web workflow state via defined mapping rules. The EMIS-X and EMIS Web workflow models are not equivalent and mapping is handled by integration logic. *(Must Have)*

