## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-002:** Patient Data Audit Trail — filing action audited before document is committed to patient record
- **CLIN-007:** Hazard Mitigation Evidence — mandatory field enforcement is the primary UI control preventing incomplete filing
- **CLIN-010:** Error Handling Patient Safety — filing must fail closed if mandatory fields are absent; never file an incomplete document silently

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-036:** Document filed with incorrect or missing metadata — document unfindable or misattributed; clinical decision made on incomplete information
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Medium
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-037:** AI/OCR metadata suggestion accepted without review — incorrect metadata auto-filed; wrong document type or date in patient record
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Medium (if suggestions auto-accepted)
  - **Risk Level:** High — **OCR/AI suggestions must never be auto-accepted**

- **HAZ-DOC-038:** Document filed against wrong patient due to unconfirmed match (cross-reference HAZ-DOC-032 from REQ-011)
  - **Severity:** Critical
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** Critical

- **HAZ-DOC-046:** Auto-routed document has incorrect embedded metadata (trusted but wrong at source) — document appears on patient record with incorrect type, date, or title in Provisional state before tasking review
  - **Severity:** Medium
  - **Likelihood:** Low (structured inbound sources are generally reliable; error would originate at the sending system)
  - **Risk Level:** Medium — mitigated by Provisional status and mandatory tasking review step

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-035:** Mandatory fields enforced at submission; filing blocked if any mandatory field is empty
  - **Type:** Business Logic + UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-036:** AI/OCR suggestions clearly labelled; user must explicitly confirm each suggested value before filing
  - **Type:** UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-037:** Patient match confirmation required before filing panel is accessible (links to REQ-011 mitigation chain)
  - **Type:** Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

