## Dimension 2: Information Governance

### Applicable Guardrails
- **IG-001:** Data Minimisation — filing form captures only the defined metadata fields; no extraneous data collected
- **IG-003:** Lawful Basis Declaration — Article 6(1)(e) public task + Article 9(2)(h) health data
- **IG-004:** Special Category Data Protection — document and associated metadata encrypted at rest on filing
- **IG-010:** Retention Policy Enforcement — filed documents subject to NHS records retention schedules from point of filing

### Data Handling
- On filing, document is written to permanent encrypted patient record store
- Document ERN generated at filing time; used as the persistent identifier for all subsequent operations
- Filing metadata (type, date, title, source, department) stored alongside document; not embedded into the document file itself
- OCR/AI suggestion inputs (document content analysed) not stored beyond the filing session

### GDPR Articles
- **Article 5(1)(d):** Accuracy — mandatory fields exist to ensure accuracy of patient record
- **Article 9(2)(h):** Special category health data — medical purposes
- **Article 5(1)(f):** Integrity and confidentiality — document protected from point of filing

