## Dimension 4: Observability & Performance

### KPIs
- Filing success rate (documents successfully filed vs. attempted)
- Mandatory field completion rate (how often users arrive at filing with fields pre-populated vs. empty)
- AI/OCR suggestion acceptance rate (proxy for suggestion quality)
- Auto-route rate (proportion of inbound documents with fully embedded metadata routed directly to tasking without manual intervention)
- Provisional document clearance time (time from auto-route to tasking action that clears Provisional status)
- Filing latency (user confirms filing → document committed to patient record)
- Incomplete filing abandonment rate (user starts filing but does not complete)

### OTEL Spans
- `documents.filing.initiated` — user opens filing panel for a document
- `documents.filing.metadata_populated` — embedded metadata auto-populated into form
- `documents.filing.suggestion_presented` — OCR/AI suggestion presented to user
- `documents.filing.suggestion_accepted` — user accepts an OCR/AI suggestion
- `documents.filing.auto_routed` — embedded-metadata document auto-routed to tasking; Provisional patient record status set
- `documents.filing.provisional_cleared` — document actioned through tasking; Provisional status removed
- `documents.filing.submitted` — user submits filing form
- `documents.filing.blocked` — filing blocked due to missing mandatory fields; missing fields recorded
- `documents.filing.completed` — document successfully filed; document ERN recorded

### SLOs
- Filing commit: p95 < 3 seconds from user submission to document filed in patient record
- Metadata auto-population: p95 < 2 seconds from document load to form pre-populated
- Filing success rate: ≥ 99.5% for submissions with all mandatory fields present

