## PxD (Added by V1d)

> **Scope: Full PxD.** UI surface: File step (Step 2 in StepIndicator) — Protocol Panel filing form. Shared components (StepIndicator, Patient Banner, Queue-Peek Sidebar) from REQ-001 reused — not re-specified here.

---

### User Flow

**Primary Flow — File a document (Step 2):**
1. Admin confirms patient match in Step 1; StepIndicator advances to Step 2 "File"
2. Protocol Panel shows filing form; Patient Banner shows matched patient
3. Fields pre-populated from OCR/AI suggestions or embedded metadata; each AI-suggested field has a disclosure hint
4. Mandatory fields: Patient (read-only — locked to matched patient), Document Type, Document Date, Document Title
5. Optional fields: Department
6. Confidentiality + Online Visibility section (defaults: Standard access / Not visible to patient)
7. Admin reviews, adjusts if needed, clicks "File document →"
8. Validation: if any mandatory field empty, inline error shown; form does not submit
9. On success: `Notification variant="success"` `{t('filing.success')}`; Step 2 tab shows ✓; Step 3 (Code) unlocks

**Error Flow — Mandatory field missing:**
- Inline `Banner variant="error"` below field: `{t('filing.error.required', { field })}`
- Error summary at top of panel if multiple fields missing
- Focus moves to first error field

**Exit Types:**
- ← Back: returns to Step 1 (Patient Match); filing not saved
- File document: completes step; advances to Step 3
- Save & close: saves current state (partial); returns to queue; document stays in Filing queue

